## Micro French Tips

Forget the wide, opaque French tip you grew up with. This season's version is thin, precise, and closer to a line drawing than a bold stripe. A <strong>micro French tip</strong> is a French manicure variation using a noticeably narrower white or coloured line along the nail edge instead of the traditional thick tip.

The shift toward a slimmer line is part of a bigger move away from maximalist nail art this year, and it fits fall particularly well because it works with darker, richer base colours in a way the classic wide tip never quite managed. Among <strong>fall nail trends 2026</strong>, it is the easiest one to translate into an office-appropriate manicure. A micro tip in cream or soft gold against a chocolate brown base looks far more current than a stark white tip against a nude base.

To ask for this at your next appointment, say "a micro French, thinner than usual, in [cream, gold, or white]" and specify the base colour underneath. It works on short and long nails equally well, since the thinner line does not compete with a shorter nail bed the way a wider tip can.

