## Cherry Wine and Deep Berry Tones

Cherry wine is the colour fall roundups keep calling "burgundy" without noticing it has actually shifted. This season's version leans cooler and more saturated, closer to an actual glass of red wine than the brick-toned burgundy that has dominated past autumns.

The appeal is obvious once you see it next to last year's palette. Cherry wine and smoky plum both carry enough depth to feel seasonal without tipping into the flat, one-note red that shows up in every generic fall listicle. It is one of the more understated entries among <strong>fall nail trends 2026</strong>, and one of the easiest to wear daily. Nail artists have been pairing these tones with both matte and glossy finishes depending on the occasion, glossy for evening, matte for daytime wear.

A single coat in cherry wine works on nearly any nail length, and it is one of the lower-maintenance trends on this list since it does not require art, layering, or a specialist tech. If pale or fair skin is a consideration, cherry wine tends to read warmer and more flattering than a true, cool-toned burgundy. Ask for it by name, since "burgundy" at most salons still defaults to the older brick shade.

