## How to Ask Your Nail Tech for These Trends

Knowing a <strong>fall nail trends 2026</strong> name is one thing. Getting your tech to execute it the way you pictured is another, and it comes down to specificity. Vague requests like "something fall-ish" get you a generic result. Specific requests, down to the finish and the accent placement, get you the actual trend.

For colour trends like mocha, cherry wine, or a chrome accent, name the exact shade family and whether you want matte or glossy. For art like tortoiseshell or plaid, specify "layered not blocked" or "thin lines, two colours" so your tech knows the current, more refined execution rather than an older, blockier version of the same trend. For the cat claw shape, ask directly whether hand-sculpted extensions are offered, since not every salon does.

