## Which Fall 2026 Nail Trend Fits Your Style

Eleven trends is a lot to hold in your head walking into an appointment, so narrow it down by what you actually want out of your hands this season. If you want something polished and low-maintenance, mocha brown or cherry wine on their own outperform anything with art attached. If you want texture without commitment, tortoiseshell or a single chrome accent nail gets you there in one sitting.

For the reader who wants to feel ahead of the curve rather than just seasonally appropriate, the cat claw shape and layered tortoiseshell are the two trends genuinely new to this year rather than refinements of an old idea. Micro French tips and plaid accents sit in between: current, but far more wearable for daily life.

Pick two, maybe three. Trying to work every trend on this list into one manicure defeats the purpose of any of them looking intentional.

